-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. GateGuard -- https://github.com/zunoworks/gateguard
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

What is reused: the deny-first-touch / demand-facts / allow-on-retry mechanism
implemented in plugins/edm/bin/edm-gateguard, and the wording of the fact
prompts that gate presents. EDM's implementation is an independent bash rewrite
(architecture.md AD1); no source file was vendored. The reused TEXT is what
this notice covers.

Specifically, in bin/edm-gateguard's gg_build_facts():
  - the Write variant's fact 1 is verbatim apart from an appended path
  - the Edit variant's fact 2 and the shared fact 3 are near-verbatim
  - the Write variant's fact 2 and the Edit variant's fact 1 are close
    paraphrases retaining long verbatim runs
  - fact 4 (quote the ticket's acceptance criteria by {PREFIX}-T{NN} ID) is
    EDM's own and has no upstream counterpart

Upstream is Python; EDM's text descends from the JavaScript port ECC vendored
at scripts/hooks/gateguard-fact-force.js, which carries GateGuard's own
attribution in its header at :19-20.

